Local fork edits for OpenBCI_32bit_SD library
=============================================

File: <Arduino libraries dir>/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/utility/Sd2Card.h
File: <Arduino libraries dir>/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/utility/Sd2Card.cpp

Change history
--------------

2026-05-13:
    SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT raised 600 ms → 1500 ms.

    Reason: pSLC / high-endurance SD cards (SanDisk Max Endurance,
    Industrial) do periodic background GC bursts that stall SPI for
    200-500 ms. At 600 ms, every overrun fires the firmware's inline 5x
    writeStart retry → ~1 s of dropped samples per GC cycle (~6
    events/min on Max Endurance 32 GB → see OBCI_B6.TXT 2026-05-13:
    e=565 r=1020). Raising to 1500 ms absorbs GC bursts up to ~1.5 s
    with NO sample loss. Worst-case downside: a truly dead-card recovery
    event takes ~1.5 s longer to declare failure, then the firmware's
    extended recovery loop in writeCache (also added 2026-05-13) takes
    over.

2026-05-15:
    SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT changed from `uint16_t const` (declared in .h with
    initialiser) to `extern uint16_t` declaration in .h plus a plain
    `uint16_t SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;` definition in .cpp.

    Reason: the firmware's new runtime tune-protocol (binary `T` wire
    command, key id 0x05; or `%TUNE sd_write_timeout=...` line in
    SESSION.TXT) rewrites SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT mid-session for A/B testing
    across nights without a reflash. A `const` would have rejected the
    write at compile time. The waitNotBusy(SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT) call sites
    all read the current value, so a tune takes effect on the next
    failed write.

    Side effect: SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT is now a memory load on every
    waitNotBusy() call instead of a compile-time constant. Negligible
    at 500 Hz sample rate; documented just in case.

Re-apply manually after any reinstall of the SD library
-------------------------------------------------------

The 2026-05-13 value bump (idempotent if already at 1500):

    sed -i 's/uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 600;/uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;/' \
        ~/Arduino/libraries/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/utility/Sd2Card.h

The 2026-05-15 const → extern conversion. Two separate edits:

  1. In Sd2Card.h, replace the `uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;`
     line with:

        extern uint16_t SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT;

     (See "Diff" below for surrounding context + comment.)

  2. In Sd2Card.cpp, add immediately after the `#include "Sd2Card.h"`
     line:

        uint16_t SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;

